    <innerclass refid="class_m2_1_1_r_element_wrap" prot="public">M2::RElementWrap</innerclass>
    <innerclass refid="class_m2_1_1_a_concrete_ring" prot="public">M2::AConcreteRing</innerclass>
    <innernamespace refid="namespace_m2">M2</innernamespace>
    <briefdescription>
<para><computeroutput>RElementWrap&lt;RingType&gt;</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>AConcreteRing&lt;RingType&gt;</computeroutput> <mdash/> abandoned scaffolding for an abstract <computeroutput><ref refid="class_a_ring" kindref="compound">ARing</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="class_r_element" kindref="compound">RElement</ref></computeroutput> base. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Declares two templates that sketch an alternative aring type-erasure design: <computeroutput>RElementWrap&lt;RingType&gt;</computeroutput> inherits from <computeroutput><ref refid="class_r_element" kindref="compound">RElement</ref></computeroutput> and stores one <computeroutput>RingType::ElementType</computeroutput> value, and <computeroutput>AConcreteRing&lt;RingType&gt;</computeroutput> inherits from <computeroutput><ref refid="class_a_ring" kindref="compound">ARing</ref></computeroutput>, holds a <computeroutput>RingType</computeroutput> by value, and forwards <computeroutput>init_set</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>add_to</computeroutput> to it through the <computeroutput>RELEM(RingType, ...)</computeroutput> cast macros. Both templates <computeroutput>friend <ref refid="classbool" kindref="compound">bool</ref> ARing::converter(const ARing*, const ARing*, const <ref refid="class_r_element" kindref="compound">RElement</ref>&amp;, <ref refid="class_r_element" kindref="compound">RElement</ref>&amp;)</computeroutput> <mdash/> but neither <computeroutput><ref refid="class_r_element" kindref="compound">RElement</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="class_a_ring" kindref="compound">ARing</ref></computeroutput>, nor <computeroutput>ARing::converter</computeroutput> is defined anywhere in the engine tree; the two templates are not referenced by any other file. Treat this header as orphan scaffolding kept around for historical / sketch purposes rather than as part of the live aring framework, whose actual ring- and element-level bridges live in <computeroutput><ref refid="aring-glue_8hpp" kindref="compound">aring-glue.hpp</ref></computeroutput> (vertical bridge to <computeroutput>Ring*</computeroutput>) and the <computeroutput>mypromote</computeroutput> / <computeroutput>mylift</computeroutput> family in <computeroutput><ref refid="aring-translate_8hpp" kindref="compound">aring-translate.hpp</ref></computeroutput>.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="aring_8hpp" kindref="compound">aring.hpp</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="aring-glue_8hpp" kindref="compound">aring-glue.hpp</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="aring-translate_8hpp" kindref="compound">aring-translate.hpp</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
